Z||000000||beachbomb||06-05-2000||07:46 PM||||Hi all! Today i started hearing a noise coming my front end. It sound just like the noise you hear from a truck that has mud tires on it going down the road. The noise starts at about 30mph and continues. Its not brake or suspension related(i think), any clues?. Its a 1984 Indy Fiero. Tires are only one month old! Thanks!||||reg||5
Z||000001||V8Fiero||06-05-2000||08:04 PM||||Check your wheel bearings. Mine are making the same noise. Not that expensive of a fix.<P>Hope this helps||||reg||7
Z||000002||beachbomb||06-05-2000||08:46 PM||||HI, would they be doing this after i just had the wheel bearings checked and packed a month ago? plmk, thanks..jim||||reg||5
Z||000003||2birds||06-05-2000||10:36 PM||||How well do you trust the guy that did the bearing work?  If they are the cause I would fix it quick before you trash a spindle. <BR>One way to check them would be to pull the calipers off and spin the wheel/rotor, to check for the noise and drag.  If it goes away, it may also be the brake pads dragging, due to sticking calipers or contaminated/poor quality pads.||||reg||1
